y week  set aside time every weekend to  synthesize all the substantive law and  your case notes and put it into an  outline it's gonna save you a huge  amount of time people say that you need  context to understand that's total crap  you will forget what is covered so it's  better to create your outlines while  it's still fresh in your mind and just  get it over with when the semester is  over if you need to redo parts of your  outline it's much easier to redo the  outline than it is to start from scratch  and most likely what will happen is that  if you do it every week instead of  waiting till the end you will have an  entire outline that's done so that you  can hit the ground running with practice  tests and memorizing law during  study period instead of starting from  scratch on your outlines it'll save you  a huge amount of time context is  overrated just start and iterate from  there people say that you study by  building your outline and while that's  true it's not like you're ignoring that  work by doing the your outline every  single week you're just getting that  done ahead of time so you can put more  time into memorizing the law and doing  your practice tests so you'll be way  ahead of everybody else who waits till  the end of the semester to do their  outline if you like this video please  click like and subscribe for more law  school crushing tips also please  download the checklist below for more  good advice so you can avoid all of the  terrible advice that's out there thanks  for stopping by  [Music]
 

